# CODEOWNERS
#
# This file defines who is automatically requested as a reviewer when a pull request
# touches specific parts of the codebase. GitHub reads this file from top to bottom;
# the LAST matching rule wins for a given file.
#
# Format: <pattern>  <owner1>  <owner2> ...
# Docs:   https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
#
# ── HOW TO USE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Replace dev-user-1 through dev-user-8 with the actual GitHub usernames of your
# team members (without the @ sign). Adjust ownership per directory as your team
# naturally divides responsibilities over time.
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Default: any file not matched by a more specific rule below requires
# a review from at least one of these owners.
